{"record_id":"D49-B63-R001","dataset_id":"D49","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","batch":"B63","topic":"Resource and Security Isolation Acceptance","subtopic":"Isolation boundary","concept":"Acceptance must verify that protected resources cannot be accessed or modified across an explicitly prohibited isolation boundary.","knowledge_type":"SECURITY_CASE","language":"English","language_version":"N/A","framework":"N/A","objective":"Verify requirement-defined resource and security isolation.","requirements":["The protected boundary must be explicitly identified.","Cross-boundary access or modification must have an observable prohibited outcome.","The tested resources must be attributable to the relevant isolation context."],"constraints":["Isolation acceptance must be tested behaviorally where possible.","A deployment topology description alone does not prove runtime isolation."],"prerequisites":["Isolation requirement","Protected resources","Cross-boundary test cases"],"dependencies":["D49-B61-R003","D49-B64-R001"],"input":{"source_context":"isolation_context_a","target_resource":"resource_in_context_b","operation":"cross_boundary_operation"},"output":{"acceptance_decision":"PASS|FAIL|UNRESOLVED"},"expected_behavior":"The prohibited cross-boundary operation is rejected or otherwise contained according to the requirement.","correct_example":{"criterion":"Acceptance passes when a subject or component from Context A cannot perform the prohibited operation against protected Resource B."},"incorrect_example":{"criterion":"Resources are isolated.","failure_reason":"No boundary or observable test is defined."},"correction":"Define source context, protected target, operation, and required isolation outcome.","failure_mode":"Cross-boundary access succeeds despite an isolation requirement.","expected_error":"ACCEPTANCE_FAIL","security_implication":"Isolation failures can enable unauthorized access, interference, or data exposure.","performance_implication":"Isolatio