{"record_id":"D49-B65-R002","dataset_id":"D49","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","batch":"B65","topic":"Cost and Budget Acceptance","subtopic":"Cost measurement integrity","concept":"Cost acceptance evidence must use a defined measurement scope, accounting basis, workload, time period, and source of cost data.","knowledge_type":"VERIFICATION_RULE","language":"English","objective":"Ensure cost acceptance decisions are based on reconstructable measurements.","requirements":["The cost source must be identifiable.","The measurement period and scope must be explicit.","The accounting basis must be defined by the requirement or measurement method."],"constraints":["Estimated cost must not be represented as measured cost.","Incomplete cost data must result in unresolved acceptance when material."],"prerequisites":["Cost requirement","Cost measurement source","Measurement definition"],"dependencies":["D49-B65-R001","D49-B13-R001"],"input":{"cost_evidence":"captured_cost_measurement","requirement":"cost_acceptance_requirement"},"output":{"acceptance_decision":"PASS|FAIL|UNRESOLVED","measurement_status":"MEASURED|ESTIMATED|INFERRED|UNKNOWN"},"expected_behavior":"The evidence clearly distinguishes measured cost from estimates or inference and supports the acceptance decision.","correct_example":{"criterion":"Acceptance passes only when measured cost evidence matches the required scope and period; estimates remain explicitly labeled."},"incorrect_example":{"criterion":"Expected monthly cost is under budget.","failure_reason":"An expectation or estimate is presented as acceptance evidence."},"correction":"Record measurement provenance and status before evaluating the threshold.","failure_mode":"An estimate is treated as observed cost evidence.","expected_error":"ACCEPTANCE_UNRESOLVED","security_implication":"Incorrect cost evidence can obscure resource-abuse or budget-control requirements when such controls are explicitly defined.","performance_implication":"Cost me