{"record_id":"D49-B65-R003","dataset_id":"D49","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","batch":"B65","topic":"Cost and Budget Acceptance","subtopic":"Budget overrun acceptance","concept":"Where a requirement defines a hard budget ceiling, acceptance must explicitly fail when verified cost exceeds that ceiling unless an approved exception path is part of the requirement.","knowledge_type":"VERIFICATION_RULE","language":"English","objective":"Verify explicit budget ceiling behavior.","requirements":["The budget ceiling must be defined.","The measured cost must use the requirement-defined scope and accounting method.","Approved exception conditions must be explicitly represented if applicable."],"constraints":["No exception may be inferred from operational convenience.","Unmeasured overrun cannot be classified as verified failure."],"prerequisites":["Budget requirement","Cost evidence","Exception policy if applicable"],"dependencies":["D49-B65-R001","D49-B86-R001"],"input":{"budget_ceiling":"defined_limit","observed_cost":"measured_cost","exception":"defined_exception_state"},"output":{"acceptance_decision":"PASS|FAIL|UNRESOLVED"},"expected_behavior":"The acceptance decision follows the explicit budget ceiling and documented exception rules.","correct_example":{"criterion":"If verified cost exceeds the hard ceiling and no valid exception applies, acceptance must fail."},"incorrect_example":{"criterion":"Budget should generally be respected.","failure_reason":"The requirement is not an enforceable acceptance condition."},"correction":"Define the ceiling, measurement scope, failure boundary, and approved exception mechanism.","failure_mode":"A verified budget overrun is accepted without a requirement-defined exception.","expected_error":"ACCEPTANCE_FAIL","security_implication":"Budget overrun can become security-relevant only when the requirement explicitly treats uncontrolled spend as a security or abuse boundary.","performance_implication":"Budget limits can constrain resource usage but do not establish a performance target by themselves.","testing_method":"Evaluate cost evidence against the hard budget boundary under both within-budget and over-budget cases.","test_input":{"within_budget":"cost_below_ceiling","over_budget":"cost_above_ceiling"},"expected_test_result":"Within-boundary cases pass and prohibited overruns fail unless a valid exception applies.","verification_method":"Apply deterministic threshold and exception evaluation to verified cost evidence.","validation_status":"GENERATED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","evidence_level":"METHODOLOGY","confidence":"HIGH","provenance":"structured_requirement_acceptance_methodology","relationships":[{"type":"refines","target":"D49-B65-R001"},{"type":"related_to","target":"D49-B86-R001"}],"related_records":["D49-B65-R001","D49-B86-R001"]}

{"record_id":"D49-B65-R004","dataset_id":"D49","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","batch":"B65","topic":"Cost and Budget Acceptance","subtopic":"Cost behavior under required workload","concept":"When cost acceptance is workload-dependent, the criterion must bind cost evaluation to the requirement-defined workload and operating conditions.","knowledge_type":"VERIFICATION_RULE","language":"English","objective":"Prevent cost acceptance from being generalized across materially different workloads.","requirements":["The acceptance workload must be explicitly defined.","Relevant operating conditions must be identified.","Cost evidence must correspond to the tested workload."],"constraints":["A cost result from one workload cannot prove another workload without an explicit equivalence basis.","Workload equivalence must be evidenced when used."],"prerequisites":["Workload-specific cost requirement","Defined operating conditions","Cost measurement"],"dependencies":["D49-B65-R001","D49-B66-R001"],"input":{"workload":"required_workload","conditions":"defined_conditions","cost_measurement":"observed_cost"},"output":{"acceptance_decision":"PASS|FAIL|UNRESOLVED"},"expected_behavior":"Cost satisfies the criterion for the exact workload and conditions required by the acceptance requirement.","correct_example":{"criterion":"Acceptance passes only when cost measured under the specified workload and conditions remains within the defined boundary."},"incorrect_example":{"criterion":"The application stays under budget.","failure_reason":"The workload and operating conditions are unspecified."},"correction":"Bind the budget criterion to an explicit workload and measurement scope.","failure_mode":"Low-workload evidence is used to accept a high-workload requirement.","expected_error":"ACCEPTANCE_UNRESOLVED","security_implication":"Workload-dependent spend can become an abuse boundary when explicitly required, but no security conclusion is implied otherwise.","performance_implication":"Cost acceptance may be correlated with resource consumption but does not replace performance acceptance.","testing_method":"Execute the specified workload and capture cost evidence under the defined conditions.","test_input":{"workload":"requirement_defined_workload","conditions":"requirement_defined_conditions"},"expected_test_result":"Measured cost remains within the requirement-defined boundary.","verification_method":"Verify workload identity, operating conditions, cost measurement, and threshold evaluation.","validation_status":"GENERATED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","evidence_level":"METHODOLOGY","confidence":"HIGH","provenance":"structured_requirement_acceptance_methodology","relationships":[{"type":"refines","target":"D49-B65-R001"},{"type":"related_to","target":"D49-B66-R001"}],"related_records":["D49-B65-R001","D49-B66-R001"]}

{"record_id":"D49-B65-R005","dataset_id":"D49","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","batch":"B65","topic":"Cost and Budget Acceptance","subtopic":"Cost acceptance evidence integrity","concept":"Cost acceptance evidence must preserve the relationship between requirement, workload, measurement method, observed cost, accounting scope, and acceptance decision.","knowledge_type":"VERIFICATION_RULE","language":"English","objective":"Make cost acceptance decisions auditable and reproducible.","requirements":["Evidence must identify the governing cost requirement.","Workload and period must be recorded.","Observed cost and measurement status must be recorded."],"constraints":["Estimated or inferred cost must remain labeled as such.","Missing accounting scope must prevent definitive acceptance when material."],"prerequisites":["Cost acceptance case","Evidence capture"],"dependencies":["D49-B13-R001","D49-B65-R001"],"input":{"test_case":"cost_acceptance_case","evidence":"captured_cost_evidence"},"output":{"acceptance_decision":"PASS|FAIL|UNRESOLVED","evidence_integrity":"SUFFICIENT|INSUFFICIENT"},"expected_behavior":"Evidence permits independent reconstruction of the cost acceptance decision.","correct_example":{"criterion":"Acceptance passes only when requirement, workload, period, accounting scope, measurement status, and observed cost are evidenced."},"incorrect_example":{"criterion":"Cost test passed.","failure_reason":"The measurement context is absent."},"correction":"Bind the decision to complete cost measurement evidence.","failure_mode":"Acceptance cannot be independently reconstructed from the recorded evidence.","expected_error":"ACCEPTANCE_UNRESOLVED","security_implication":"Weak evidence can conceal requirement-defined spend-control failures.","performance_implication":"Cost evidence may use performance/resource measurements, but no performance conclusion is implied.","testing_method":"Inspect cost evidence for completeness, provenance, and scope alignment.","test_input":{"required_evidence":["requirement","workload","period","accounting_scope","measurement_status","observed_cost"]},"expected_test_result":"All required evidence is present and internally consistent.","verification_method":"Run evidence completeness, provenance, and measurement-status validation.","validation_status":"GENERATED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","evidence_level":"METHODOLOGY","confidence":"HIGH","provenance":"structured_requirement_acceptance_methodology","relationships":[{"type":"requires","target":"D49-B13-R001"},{"type":"verifies","target":"D49-B65-R001"}],"related_records":["D49-B13-R001","D49-B65-R001"]}

{"record_id":"D49-B66-R001","dataset_id":"D49","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","batch":"B66","topic":"Capacity and Scaling Acceptance","subtopic":"Capacity threshold acceptance","concept":"Capacity acceptance must verify the requirement-defined workload boundary and the required system behavior at that boundary.","knowledge_type":"PERFORMANCE_CASE","language":"English","objective":"Verify explicit capacity requirements without inventing universal capacity limits.","requirements":["The required workload or capacity target must be defined.","Acceptance behavior at, below, and where required beyond the boundary must be specified.","Measurement conditions must be defined."],"constraints":["No capacity threshold is assumed without a requirement.","Capacity evidence must be tied to the tested environment and version."],"prerequisites":["Capacity requirement","Defined workload","Measurement method"],"dependencies":["D49-B16-R002","D48","D49-B65-R001"],"input":{"capacity_target":"requirement_defined_target","workload":"defined_workload","environment":"identified_environment"},"output":{"acceptance_decision":"PASS|FAIL|UNRESOLVED","observed_capacity":"measured_capacity"},"expected_behavior":"The system satisfies the required capacity boundary under the defined conditions.","correct_example":{"criterion":"Acceptance passes when the measured supported workload reaches the requirement-defined capacity while all required functional and nonfunctional conditions remain satisfied."},"incorrect_example":{"criterion":"The system supports many users.","failure_reason":"Capacity is undefined and cannot be deterministically accepted."},"correction":"Define workload units, capacity threshold, operating conditions, and pass criteria.","failure_mode":"Capacity is accepted from an unmeasured or differently scoped workload.","expected_error":"ACCEPTANCE_UNRESOLVED","security_implication":"Capacity failure can become a security concern when explicitly tied to resource-exhaustion or abuse requirements.","performance_implication":"Capacity acceptance is performance-related and must use measured or otherwise evidence-backed workload results.","testing_method":"Apply the requirement-defined workload and measure capacity and required service behavior.","test_input":{"workload":"requirement_defined_capacity_workload"},"expected_test_result":"Required capacity is achieved with all applicable acceptance conditions satisfied.","verification_method":"Compare measured capacity and associated functional/resource evidence with the requirement.","validation_status":"GENERATED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","evidence_level":"METHODOLOGY","confidence":"HIGH","provenance":"structured_requirement_acceptance_methodology","relationships":[{"type":"verifies","target":"D49-B16-R002"},{"type":"related_to","target":"D48"},{"type":"related_to","target":"D49-B65-R001"}],"related_records":["D49-B16-R002","D48","D49-B65-R001"]}

{"record_id":"D49-B66-R002","dataset_id":"D49","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","batch":"B66","topic":"Capacity and Scaling Acceptance","subtopic":"Scaling transition acceptance","concept":"Acceptance must verify that scaling transitions preserve the requirement-defined behavior, integrity, and capacity boundary.","knowledge_type":"VERIFICATION_RULE","language":"English","objective":"Verify acceptance across defined scaling transitions.","requirements":["Scaling trigger or transition condition must be defined.","Pre-scale and post-scale acceptance conditions must be specified.","Relevant state and data integrity requirements must remain applicable."],"constraints":["Scaling success does not automatically prove application correctness.","Only requirement-defined scaling behavior should be accepted."],"prerequisites":["Scaling requirement","Controlled scaling mechanism","Representative workload"],"dependencies":["D49-B66-R001","D49-B18-R001","D49-B49-R001"],"input":{"initial_capacity":"defined_initial_state","scaling_event":"defined_scaling_transition","workload":"required_workload"},"output":{"acceptance_decision":"PASS|FAIL|UNRESOLVED"},"expected_behavior":"The scaling transition achieves the required capacity or resource state without violating functional, integrity, or security acceptance conditions.","correct_example":{"criterion":"Acceptance passes when the defined scaling event completes and post-scale service behavior remains within all applicable requirements."},"incorrect_example":{"criterion":"Autoscaling worked.","failure_reason":"No measurable post-scale acceptance condition is specified."},"correction":"Define trigger, target state, workload, and post-transition acceptance criteria.","failure_mode":"Scaling increases resources but violates correctness, integrity, or availability requirements.","expected_error":"ACCEPTANCE_FAIL","security_implication":"Incorrect scaling behavior can expand attack surface or create resource-exhaustion conditi