{"record_id":"D49-B66-R003","dataset_id":"D49","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","batch":"B66","topic":"Capacity and Scaling Acceptance","subtopic":"Capacity degradation boundary","concept":"Where requirements define degraded behavior under capacity pressure, acceptance must distinguish acceptable degradation from prohibited failure.","knowledge_type":"PERFORMANCE_CASE","language":"English","objective":"Verify explicit capacity-pressure behavior.","requirements":["The capacity-pressure condition must be defined.","Acceptable degraded behavior must be explicitly stated.","Prohibited failure states must be identifiable."],"constraints":["Degradation thresholds must not be invented.","A system remaining responsive is insufficient if the requirement defines stronger behavior."],"prerequisites":["Capacity-pressure requirement","Defined stress condition","Observable service metrics or outcomes"],"dependencies":["D49-B48-R001","D49-B66-R001"],"input":{"pressure_condition":"requirement_defined_capacity_pressure","observations":"service_behavior_under_pressure"},"output":{"acceptance_decision":"PASS|FAIL|UNRESOLVED"},"expected_behavior":"Under the defined capacity pressure, the system remains within the requirement-defined acceptable behavior boundary.","correct_example":{"criterion":"Acceptance passes when measured degradation remains within the specified boundary and prohibited failure modes do not occur."},"incorrect_example":{"criterion":"The system handles overload gracefully.","failure_reason":"Graceful behavior is undefined."},"correction":"Define measurable degradation limits and prohibited failure states.","failure_mode":"Capacity pressure produces behavior beyond the accepted degradation boundary.","expected_error":"ACCEPTANCE_FAIL","security_implication":"Capacity pressure can expose denial-of-service weaknesses when such behavior is part of the security requirement.","performance_implication":"This criterion requires evidence-backed measurement of the specified degradation boundary.","testing_method":"Apply the requirement-defined capacity pressure and observe relevant metrics and failure modes.","test_input":{"load":"defined_pressure_condition"},"expected_test_result":"All observed behavior remains within the accepted degradation boundary.","verification_method":"Evaluate measured observations against explicit capacity-pressure acceptance thresholds.","validation_status":"GENERATED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","evidence_level":"METHODOLOGY","confidence":"HIGH","provenance":"structured_requirement_acceptance_methodology","relationships":[{"type":"related_to","target":"D49-B48-R001"},{"type":"refines","target":"D49-B66-R001"}],"related_records":["D49-B48-R001","D49-B66-R001"]}

{"record_id":"D49-B66-R004","dataset_id":"D49","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","batch":"B66","topic":"Capacity and Scaling Acceptance","subtopic":"Capacity recovery acceptance","concept":"When a capacity requirement includes recovery after resource pressure, acceptance must verify return to the required service boundary after the pressure condition ends.","knowledge_type":"VERIFICATION_RULE","language":"English","objective":"Verify post-pressure capacity recovery where required.","requirements":["The pressure condition and recovery trigger must be defined.","The required recovery state or threshold must be explicit.","Recovery measurement conditions must be specified."],"constraints":["Recovery time or capacity target must not be invented.","A return to service availability alone does not prove recovery to the required capacity."],"prerequisites":["Capacity recovery requirement","Controlled pressure condition","Recovery measurement"],"dependencies":["D49-B19-R001","D49-B66-R001"],"input":{"pressure_event":"defined_capacity_pressure","recovery_trigger":"defined_recovery_condition","target":"required_recovered_capacity"},"output":{"acceptance_decision":"PASS|FAIL|UNRESOLVED","recovery_observation":"measured_recovery"},"expected_behavior":"The system returns to the requirement-defined capacity or resource state within the accepted boundary.","correct_example":{"criterion":"Acceptance passes when the system reaches the required recovered capacity within the explicitly defined recovery condition."},"incorrect_example":{"criterion":"The system recovers after overload.","failure_reason":"Recovery target and boundary are unspecified."},"correction":"Define recovery target, trigger, timing or state boundary, and measurement method.","failure_mode":"Service resumes but remains below the required capacity boundary.","expected_error":"ACCEPTANCE_FAIL","security_implication":"Incomplete recovery can extend resource-exhaustion impact when relevant to security requirements.","performance_implication":"Recovery acceptance requires evidence-backed capacity or resource measurements.","testing_method":"Apply pressure, remove it according to the defined trigger, and measure recovery.","test_input":{"pressure":"defined_pressure","recovery":"defined_recovery_trigger"},"expected_test_result":"Measured recovery reaches the requirement-defined target.","verification_method":"Compare recovery measurements with the requirement-defined target and boundary.","validation_status":"GENERATED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","evidence_level":"METHODOLOGY","confidence":"HIGH","provenance":"structured_requirement_acceptance_methodology","relationships":[{"type":"related_to","target":"D49-B19-R001"},{"type":"refines","target":"D49-B66-R001"}],"related_records":["D49-B19-R001","D49-B66-R001"]}

{"record_id":"D49-B66-R005","dataset_id":"D49","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","batch":"B66","topic":"Capacity and Scaling Acceptance","subtopic":"Capacity evidence integrity","concept":"Capacity acceptance evidence must preserve workload, environment, software version, measurement method, observed capacity, and acceptance decision.","knowledge_type":"VERIFICATION_RULE","language":"English","objective":"Ensure capacity acceptance is reconstructable and comparable.","requirements":["Workload must be identifiable.","Environment and software version must be recorded.","Measurement method and observed capacity must be recorded."],"constraints":["Capacity evidence from a materially different workload or environment cannot directly prove the current requirement.","Estimated capacity must not be represented as measured capacity."],"prerequisites":["Capacity test","Evidence capture"],"dependencies":["D49-B13-R001","D49-B66-R001"],"input":{"test_case":"capacity_acceptance_case","evidence":"captured_capacity_evidence"},"output":{"acceptance_decision":"PASS|FAIL|UNRESOLVED","evidence_integrity":"SUFFICIENT|INSUFFICIENT"},"expected_behavior":"Evidence is sufficient to reconstruct the capacity acceptance decision and its measurement context.","correct_example":{"criterion":"Acceptance passes only when workload, environment, version, measurement method, observed capacity, and decision are evidenced."},"incorrect_example":{"criterion":"Capacity test passed.","failure_reason":"The workload and environment are absent."},"correction":"Bind capacity acceptance to structured measurement evidence.","failure_mode":"Capacity acceptance is generalized from incompatible evidence.","expected_error":"ACCEPTANCE_UNRESOLVED","security_implication":"Weak capacity evidence can conceal resource-exhaustion boundaries when those are requirement-defined.","performance_implication":"Capacity evidence must preserve measurement semantics to support valid performance conclusions.","testing_method":"Inspect capacity evidence for scope, provenance, version, and measurement completeness.","test_input":{"required_evidence":["workload","environment","software_version","measurement_method","observed_capacity"]},"expected_test_result":"Required capacity evidence is complete and internally consistent.","verification_method":"Perform evidence completeness, version alignment, workload alignment, and measurement-status checks.","validation_status":"GENERATED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","evidence_level":"METHODOLOGY","confidence":"HIGH","provenance":"structured_requirement_acceptance_methodology","relationships":[{"type":"requires","target":"D49-B13-R001"},{"type":"verifies","target":"D49-B66-R001"}],"related_records":["D49-B13-R001","D49-B66-R001"]}

{"record_id":"D49-B67-R001","dataset_id":"D49","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","batch":"B67","topic":"Performance Regression Acceptance","subtopic":"Baseline comparison","concept":"Performance regression acceptance requires a valid baseline and an explicit comparison criterion defined by the requirement.","knowledge_type":"PERFORMANCE_CASE","language":"English","objective":"Verify that performance changes are evaluated against an appropriate baseline.","requirements":["Baseline version or measurement must be identifiable.","Workload and environment must be comparable or equivalence must be established.","Regression threshold must be requirement-defined."],"constraints":["No universal regression percentage is assumed.","A baseline from a materially different environment cannot directly establish regression without evidence of comparability."],"prerequisites":["Performance requirement","Baseline evidence","Current performance measurement"],"dependencies":["D48","D49-B16-R001"],"input":{"baseline":"identified_baseline_measurement","candidate":"current_measurement","comparison":"defined_regression_rule"},"output":{"acceptance_decision":"PASS|FAIL|UNRESOLVED","regression_status":"NO_REGRESSION|REGRESSION|UNRESOLVED"},"expected_behavior":"The comparison follows the requirement-defined baseline and regression rule.","correct_example":{"criterion":"Acceptance fails when the current measured latency exceeds the explicit regression threshold relative to a valid comparable baseline."},"incorrect_example":{"criterion":"Performance is worse than before.","failure_reason":"The baseline, workload, and threshold are unspecified."},"correction":"Define baseline identity, workload, environment, metric, and regression threshold.","failure_mode":"Performance regression is accepted or rejected using an invalid baseline.","expected_error":"ACCEPTANCE_UNRESOLVED","security_implication":"Performance regression may affect security controls only when a requirement explicitly depends on performance behavior.","performance_implication":"This criterion directly evaluates performance regression using evidence-backed measurements.","testing_method":"Repeat the defined performance case under comparable conditions and compare measurements using the specified regression rule.","test_input":{"baseline":"valid_baseline","candidate":"current_measurement"},"expected_test_result":"Regression status is deterministically evaluated from the requirement-defined comparison.","verification_method":"Validate baseline comparability and apply the explicit regression criterion.","validation_status":"GENERATED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","evidence_level":"METHODOLOGY","confidence":"HIGH","provenance":"structured_requirement_acceptance_methodology","relationships":[{"type":"related_to","target":"D48"},{"type":"verifies","target":"D49-B16-R001"}],"related_records":["D48","D49-B16-R001"]}

{"record_id":"D49-B67-R002","dataset_id":"D49","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","batch":"B67","topic":"Performance Regression Acceptance","subtopic":"Regression evidence comparability","concept":"Performance regression acceptance requires alignment of workload, environment, software version, configuration, measurement method, and metric definition between baseline and candidate evidence.","knowledge_type":"VERIFICATION_RULE","language":"English","objective":"Prevent false regression decisions caused by incomparable measurements.","requirements":["Baseline and candidate measurement contexts must be identifiable.","Material differences must be documented and addressed by the acceptance method."],"constraints":["Different environments cannot be treated as equivalent without evidence.","Measurement-definition changes must be accounted for before comparison."],"prerequisites":["Baseline measurement","Candidate measurement","Context metadata"],"dependencies":["D49-B67-R001","D49-B14-R005"],"input":{"baseline_context":"baseline_metadata","candidate_context":"candidate_metadata"},"output":{"acceptance_decision":"PASS|FAIL|UNRESOLVED","comparability":"COMPARABLE|NOT_COMPARABLE|UNRESOLVED"},"expected_behavior":"The regression comparison proceeds only when the evidence is sufficiently comparable for the defined criterion.","correct_example":{"criterion":"Acceptance is unresolved when a material workload or environment difference prevents valid comparison and no equivalence evidence exists."},"incorrect_example":{"criterion":"Both tests ran successfully, so the results are comparable.","failure_reason":"Execution success does not establish measurement comparability."},"correction":"Validate comparison context before applying the regression threshold.","failure_mode":"An apparent regression or improvement is caused by changed measurement conditions.","expected_error":"ACCEPTANCE_UNRESOLVED","security_implication":"False performance acceptance can hide degraded security-control behavior when performance is security-relevant.","performance_implication":"Measurement comparability is foundational to valid regression conclusions.","testing_method":"Compare baseline and candidate metadata before comparing performance values.","test_input":{"baseline_context":"captured_context","candidate_context":"captured_context"},"expected_test_result":"Context is comparable or an explicit equivalence basis exists.","verification_method":"Run structured metadata comparison and reject unsupported equivalence.","validation_status":"GENERATED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","evidence_level":"METHODOLOGY","confidence":"HIGH","provenance":"structured_requirement_acceptance_methodology","relationships":[{"type":"refines","target":"D49-B67-R001"},{"type":"related_to","target":"D49-B14-R005"}],"related_records":["D49-B67-R001","D49-B14-R005"]}

{"record_id":"D49-B67-R003","dataset_id":"D49","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","batch":"B67","topic":"Performance Regression Acceptance","subtopic":"Regression threshold acceptance","concept":"Acceptance must apply the explicitly defined performance regression threshold consistently across the requirement's applicable measurements.","knowledge_type":"VERIFICATION_RULE","language":"English","objective":"Verify deterministic performance regression decisioning.","requirements":["Metric must be defined.","Baseline and candidate values must be measured or otherwise evidence-backed.","Regression threshold and comparison direction must be explicit."],"constraints":["Thresholds must not be invented from generic practice.","Metric aggregation rules must be defined when multiple observations are used."],"prerequisites":["Regression requirement","Comparable baseline and candidate evidence","Defined evaluation rule"],"dependencies":["D49-B67-R001","D49-B67-R002"],"input":{"metric":"defined_performance_metric","baseline_value":"baseline_value","candidate_value":"candidate_value","threshold":"requirement_defined_threshold"},"output":{"acceptance_decision":"PASS|FAIL|UNRESOLVED"},"expected_behavior":"The acceptance decision follows the exact threshold and aggregation rule defined by the requirement.","correct_example":{"criterion":"If the defined candidate metric violates the requirement threshold relative to the baseline, acceptance fails."},"incorrect_example":{"criterion":"Small performance changes are acceptable.","failure_reason":"Small is not defined."},"correction":"Specify the exact metric, comparison rule, threshold, and aggregation method.","failure_mode":"Different evaluators produce different regression decisions from identical evidence.","expected_error":"ACCEPTANCE_INDETERMINATE","security_implication":"Inconsistent regression decisions can permit unreviewed degradation of security-relevant performance.","performance_implication":"The criterion directly evaluates measured performance change against an explicit threshold.","testing_method":"Apply the defined threshold to controlled baseline and candidate measurements.","test_input":{"baseline":"measured_baseline","candidate":"measured_candidate"},"expected_test_result":"Decision is deterministic and reproducible.","verification_method":"Recompute the acceptance decision independently from recorded values and rule.","validation_status":"GENERATED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","evidence_level":"METHODOLOGY","confidence":"HIGH","provenance":"structured_requirement_acceptance_methodology","relationships":[{"type":"refines","target":"D49-B67-R001"},{"type":"requires","target":"D49-B67-R002"}],"related_records":["D49-B67-R001","D49-B67-R002"]}

{"record_id":"D49-B67-R004","dataset_id":"D49","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","batch":"B67","topic":"Performance Regression Acceptance","subtopic":"Regression false-positive and false-negative handling","concept":"Acceptance must distinguish genuine performance regression from measurement noise, environment drift, and insufficient evidence.","knowledge_type":"FAILURE_MODE","language":"English","objective":"Prevent unsupported regression decisions.","requirements":["The acceptance method must define treatment of variability or uncertainty where material.","Evidence must support the distinction between regression and measurement uncertainty."],"constraints":["Statistical conclusions require appropriate data and method.","A single observation must not be treated as definitive when the requirement requires repeated measurement."],"prerequisites":["Regression requirement","Measurement variability information","Defined evaluation method"],"dependencies":["D49-B67-R001","D49-B78-R001"],"input":{"observations":"performance_measurements","uncertainty":"measurement_or_sampling_context"},"output":{"acceptance_decision":"PASS|FAIL|UNRESOLVED"},"expected_behavior":"Acceptance reflects the defined evidence and uncertainty rules rather than unsupported interpretation.","correct_example":{"criterion":"Acceptance remains unresolved when evidence cannot distinguish the measured change from the requirement-defined uncertainty boundary."},"incorrect_example":{"criterion":"One slower run proves a regression.","failure_reason":"The evidence may be insufficient for the requirement's decision rule."},"correction":"Define repetition, aggregation, uncertainty, and decision rules where required.","failure_mode":"Noise is accepted as regression or genuine regression is dismissed as noise without evidence.","expected_error":"ACCEPTANCE_UNRESOLVED","security_implication":"Incorrect performance decisions can conceal degradation of security-relevant functions.","performance_implica