{"record_id":"D49-B67-R005","dataset_id":"D49","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","batch":"B67","topic":"Performance Regression Acceptance","subtopic":"Regression evidence integrity","concept":"Performance regression acceptance evidence must preserve baseline identity, candidate identity, workload, environment, version, metric, measurements, evaluation rule, and final decision.","knowledge_type":"VERIFICATION_RULE","language":"English","objective":"Ensure performance regression decisions are auditable and reproducible.","requirements":["Baseline and candidate identities must be recorded.","Measurement contexts and values must be preserved.","Decision rule and result must be reconstructable."],"constraints":["Unsupported or incomplete evidence must remain unresolved.","Estimated performance values must remain explicitly labeled."],"prerequisites":["Regression acceptance case","Evidence capture"],"dependencies":["D49-B13-R001","D49-B67-R001"],"input":{"test_case":"performance_regression_case","evidence":"captured_regression_evidence"},"output":{"acceptance_decision":"PASS|FAIL|UNRESOLVED","evidence_integrity":"SUFFICIENT|INSUFFICIENT"},"expected_behavior":"The complete regression decision can be independently recomputed from the evidence.","correct_example":{"criterion":"Acceptance passes only when baseline, candidate, context, metric, values, rule, and result are preserved."},"incorrect_example":{"criterion":"Regression check passed.","failure_reason":"The evidence needed to reproduce the decision is absent."},"correction":"Store structured regression evidence and the exact evaluation rule.","failure_mode":"Regression acceptance cannot be reconstructed or audited.","expected_error":"ACCEPTANCE_UNRESOLVED","security_implication":"Weak evidence integrity can conceal performance regressions affecting security controls.","performance_implication":"Evidence must preserve measurement semantics for valid performance conclusions.","testing_method":"Inspect regres