{"record_id":"D49-B68-R001","dataset_id":"D49","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","batch":"B68","topic":"Regression Acceptance Criteria","subtopic":"Functional regression acceptance","concept":"Regression acceptance requires previously satisfied requirements to remain satisfied after a change unless the requirement itself was intentionally changed.","knowledge_type":"VERIFICATION_RULE","language":"English","objective":"Verify preservation of established required behavior after change.","requirements":["Affected requirements must be identified.","Regression cases must correspond to the requirement baseline.","Intentional requirement changes must be separately versioned or traced."],"constraints":["A passing old test does not prove an unchanged requirement if the test no longer covers the requirement.","Changed requirements require updated acceptance criteria."],"prerequisites":["Change under evaluation","Existing requirement-to-test traceability","Regression cases"],"dependencies":["D49-B68-R002","D49-B90-R001"],"input":{"change":"candidate_change","baseline_requirement":"previous_requirement","regression_case":"mapped_regression_case"},"output":{"acceptance_decision":"PASS|FAIL|UNRESOLVED"},"expected_behavior":"Unchanged requirements remain satisfied after the change.","correct_example":{"criterion":"Acceptance passes when all applicable unchanged requirements continue to satisfy their mapped acceptance criteria after the change."},"incorrect_example":{"criterion":"All old tests passed.","failure_reason":"The test set may not cover all affected requirements."},"correction":"Evaluate regression coverage against affected requirements, not only historical test execution.","failure_mode":"A change breaks a requirement that was not represented by an effective regression case.","expected_error":"ACCEPTANCE_FAIL","security_implication":"Unnoticed regressions can reintroduce previously corrected security failures.","performance_implication":"Regression acceptance may include performance criteria where requirements define them; it does not assume performance equivalence universally.","testing_method":"Map changed components to affected requirements and execute their applicable regression acceptance cases.","test_input":{"change":"defined_change","affected_requirements":"impact_analysis_result"},"expected_test_result":"All applicable unchanged requirements remain accepted.","verification_method":"Verify requirement coverage, regression execution, and acceptance evidence.","validation_status":"GENERATED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","evidence_level":"METHODOLOGY","confidence":"HIGH","provenance":"structured_requirement_acceptance_methodology","relationships":[{"type":"related_to","target":"D49-B90-R001"},{"type":"requires","target":"D49-B68-R002"}],"related_records":["D49-B90-R001","D49-B68-R002"]}

{"record_id":"D49-B68-R002","dataset_id":"D49","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","batch":"B68","topic":"Regression Acceptance Criteria","subtopic":"Regression coverage acceptance","concept":"Acceptance must verify that all requirement-relevant changed areas have corresponding regression criteria or an explicitly justified unresolved gap.","knowledge_type":"VERIFICATION_RULE","language":"English","objective":"Detect missing regression acceptance coverage.","requirements":["Change impact must be assessed.","Affected requirements must map to regression criteria.","Uncovered affected requirements must be explicitly surfaced."],"constraints":["Coverage cannot be inferred solely from test count.","A regression case must actually exercise the relevant requirement behavior."],"prerequisites":["Change impact analysis","Requirement traceability","Regression suite"],"dependencies":["D49-B11-R001","D49-B11-R002","D49-B68-R001"],"input":{"change":"candidate_change","impact_map":"affected_requirements","regression_cases":"available_regression_cases"},"output":{"acceptance_decision":"PASS|FAIL|UNRESOLVED","coverage_status":"COVERED|GAP|UNRESOLVED"},"expected_behavior":"Every affected requirement has valid regression acceptance coverage or an explicitly recorded gap.","correct_example":{"criterion":"Acceptance is unresolved when an affected requirement lacks a valid regression case and no justified alternative verification exists."},"incorrect_example":{"criterion":"Regression suite is large enough.","failure_reason":"Size does not establish requirement coverage."},"correction":"Evaluate coverage through explicit requirement-to-regression relationships.","failure_mode":"A changed requirement remains untested despite a nominally large regression suite.","expected_error":"ACCEPTANCE_UNRESOLVED","security_implication":"Coverage gaps can allow security regressions to escape validation.","performance_implication":"Performance regression coverage must use performance-specific evidence where the requirement demands it.","testing_method":"Construct a change-to-requirement-to-regression coverage map and identify gaps.","test_input":{"affected_requirements":"impact_analysis","regression_cases":"candidate_suite"},"expected_test_result":"All affected requirements are covered or explicit gaps are recorded.","verification_method":"Check bidirectional traceability and requirement coverage completeness.","validation_status":"GENERATED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","evidence_level":"METHODOLOGY","confidence":"HIGH","provenance":"structured_requirement_acceptance_methodology","relationships":[{"type":"requires","target":"D49-B11-R001"},{"type":"requires","target":"D49-B11-R002"},{"type":"refines","target":"D49-B68-R001"}],"related_records":["D49-B11-R001","D49-B11-R002","D49-B68-R001"]}

{"record_id":"D49-B68-R003","dataset_id":"D49","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","batch":"B68","topic":"Regression Acceptance Criteria","subtopic":"Regression negative acceptance","concept":"Regression acceptance must include relevant negative behavior where a change could re-enable previously rejected, unsafe, or invalid operations.","knowledge_type":"SECURITY_CASE","language":"English","objective":"Verify that prohibited behavior remains prohibited after change.","requirements":["Previously prohibited behavior relevant to the change must be identified.","Negative acceptance cases must define expected rejection or containment."],"constraints":["Only relevant negative cases should be included; superficial repetition is not coverage.","A negative case must correspond to an actual requirement or documented invariant."],"prerequisites":["Change impact analysis","Negative acceptance cases","Relevant requirements"],"dependencies":["D49-B46-R001","D49-B68-R001"],"input":{"change":"candidate_change","negative_cases":"affected_negative_cases"},"output":{"acceptance_decision":"PASS|FAIL|UNRESOLVED"},"expected_behavior":"Previously prohibited behavior remains rejected or safely contained after the change.","correct_example":{"criterion":"Acceptance passes when affected negative cases continue to produce the requirement-defined rejection or containment result."},"incorrect_example":{"criterion":"The feature still works, so regression is unlikely.","failure_reason":"Functional success does not verify prohibited behavior."},"correction":"Execute requirement-linked negative regression criteria for affected boundaries.","failure_mode":"A change unintentionally re-enables a previously prohibited operation.","expected_error":"ACCEPTANCE_FAIL","security_implication":"Negative regression failures can reintroduce security vulnerabilities or unsafe behavior.","performance_implication":"Negative-case performance is relevant only when explicitly required.","testing_method":"Execute affected negative cases against the changed implementation.","test_input":{"negative_case":"requirement_prohibited_operation"},"expected_test_result":"The prohibited operation remains rejected or contained as required.","verification_method":"Compare observed behavior with the negative acceptance criterion and baseline evidence.","validation_status":"GENERATED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","evidence_level":"METHODOLOGY","confidence":"HIGH","provenance":"structured_requirement_acceptance_methodology","relationships":[{"type":"related_to","target":"D49-B46-R001"},{"type":"refines","target":"D49-B68-R001"}],"related_records":["D49-B46-R001","D49-B68-R001"]}

