{"record_id":"D49-B69-R001","dataset_id":"D49","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","batch":"B69","topic":"Release Acceptance","subtopic":"Release requirement acceptance","concept":"A release is accepted only when all release-gating requirements defined for the release are satisfied or explicitly classified under an approved exception path.","knowledge_type":"VERIFICATION_RULE","language":"English","objective":"Verify requirement-defined release readiness.","requirements":["Release scope must be identified.","Release-gating requirements must be enumerated.","Acceptance state for each gate must be determinable."],"constraints":["Release acceptance must not be inferred from test count alone.","Unresolved mandatory gates cannot be silently converted to pass."],"prerequisites":["Release candidate","Release requirements","Acceptance criteria"],"dependencies":["D49-B68-R001","D49-B70-R001"],"input":{"release":"identified_release_candidate","gates":"release_acceptance_gates"},"output":{"acceptance_decision":"PASS|FAIL|UNRESOLVED"},"expected_behavior":"The release decision reflects all mandatory requirement acceptance gates and documented exceptions.","correct_example":{"criterion":"Acceptance passes only when every mandatory release gate is satisfied with sufficient evidence or an explicitly authorized exception applies."},"incorrect_example":{"criterion":"The release looks ready.","failure_reason":"Readiness is subjective and does not define gate conditions."},"correction":"Define mandatory release gates, acceptance states, evidence requirements, and exception handling.","failure_mode":"A release is accepted despite an unresolved mandatory requirement.","expected_error":"ACCEPTANCE_FAIL","security_implication":"Release gating can prevent deployment of known unmet security requirements.","performance_implication":"Release acceptance may include performance gates where requirements explicitly define them.","testing_method":"Evaluate each release gate against its m