{"record_id":"D49-B71-R001","dataset_id":"D49","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","batch":"B71","topic":"CI/CD Acceptance Gates","subtopic":"Pipeline gate criterion","concept":"CI/CD acceptance gate must define an explicit, evidence-based condition that determines whether a pipeline stage may proceed.","knowledge_type":"VERIFICATION_RULE","language":"English","language_version":"N/A","framework":"N/A","framework_version":"N/A","objective":"Ensure required CI/CD validation conditions are satisfied before progression.","requirements":["Required gate condition is explicitly defined","Gate evaluation is deterministic or its decision rule is explicit","Evidence is attributable to the relevant pipeline execution"],"constraints":["Acceptance depends only on declared requirements and available evidence","A successful pipeline stage must not be inferred without gate evidence"],"prerequisites":["Defined CI/CD pipeline","Defined acceptance requirement","Accessible pipeline evidence"],"dependencies":["D49-B20-R002","D49-B24-R001"],"input":{"requirement":"A release pipeline must block progression when required validation fails","pipeline_execution_id":"CI-EXEC-001","gate_result":"BLOCKED","evidence":["required test suite failed"]},"output":{"acceptance_status":"PASS","decision":"REQUIREMENT_SATISFIED","evidence_required":true},"expected_behavior":"The acceptance criterion passes only when the required gate evaluates the declared condition using attributable pipeline evidence.","correct_example":{"criterion":"PASS if all mandatory validation stages complete successfully and their results are attributable to the same pipeline execution."},"incorrect_example":{"criterion":"PASS if the pipeline looks successful."},"correction":"Replace subjective pipeline appearance with explicit mandatory-stage results tied to a pipeline execution.","failure_mode":"Pipeline progression is accepted without satisfying mandatory validation gates.","expected_error":"ACCEPTANCE_GATE_EVIDENCE