{"record_id":"D49-B71-R002","dataset_id":"D49","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","batch":"B71","topic":"CI/CD Acceptance Gates","subtopic":"Mandatory test gate","concept":"A mandatory test gate must prevent acceptance when required tests have not passed.","knowledge_type":"VERIFICATION_RULE","language":"English","language_version":"N/A","framework":"N/A","framework_version":"N/A","objective":"Prevent incomplete or failed required testing from being accepted through CI/CD.","requirements":["Mandatory tests are identified","Required tests have attributable results","Failed or missing required results block acceptance"],"constraints":["Optional tests must not be silently treated as mandatory","Missing evidence is not equivalent to a passing result"],"prerequisites":["Test policy","Pipeline execution","Test result records"],"dependencies":["D42","D43","D49-B13-R002"],"input":{"required_tests":["unit","integration"],"results":{"unit":"PASS","integration":"MISSING"}},"output":{"acceptance_status":"FAIL","decision":"REQUIREMENT_NOT_SATISFIED","reason":"mandatory_test_evidence_missing"},"expected_behavior":"Acceptance fails when a mandatory test lacks a valid passing result.","correct_example":{"criterion":"PASS only when every declared mandatory test has a valid PASS result from the relevant execution."},"incorrect_example":{"criterion":"PASS when no mandatory test has an explicit FAIL result."},"correction":"Treat missing mandatory evidence as unresolved or failed according to the declared acceptance policy rather than as success.","failure_mode":"A release passes despite missing mandatory test evidence.","expected_error":"MANDATORY_TEST_EVIDENCE_MISSING","security_implication":"Missing security-test evidence may permit unvalidated changes to proceed.","performance_implication":"Required performance tests must have valid results before performance-related acceptance is granted.","testing_method":"Remove the result for one mandatory test and evaluate the gate.