{"record_id":"D49-B75-R004","dataset_id":"D49","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","batch":"B75","topic":"Reproducibility Acceptance","subtopic":"Deterministic-output acceptance","concept":"When a requirement explicitly requires deterministic output, acceptance requires repeated executions to satisfy the defined deterministic-output condition.","knowledge_type":"CONSTRAINT","language":"English","language_version":"N/A","objective":"Define acceptance for deterministic-output requirements without assuming determinism universally.","requirements":["Determinism is explicitly required","Output comparison rule is defined","Relevant execution conditions are controlled"],"constraints":["Determinism should not be imposed when the system is intentionally nondeterministic","Equivalent-result criteria may be used when exact output equality is not required"],"prerequisites":["Deterministic-output requirement","Comparison rule","Controlled execution conditions"],"dependencies":["D49-B78-R001","D49-B76-R001"],"input":{"run_1":"OUTPUT-A","run_2":"OUTPUT-A","required":"EXACT_MATCH"},"output":{"acceptance_status":"PASS"},"expected_behavior":"Acceptance passes when repeated outputs satisfy the explicitly required deterministic comparison rule.","correct_example":{"criterion":"PASS when repeated executions under required conditions produce exactly matching outputs where exact determinism is required."},"incorrect_example":{"criterion":"PASS because outputs are approximately similar when exact equality is required."},"correction":"Apply the comparison rule specified by the requirement.","failure_mode":"A deterministic-output requirement is accepted despite differing outputs.","expected_error":"DETERMINISTIC_OUTPUT_MISMATCH","security_implication":"Unexpected nondeterminism can affect security decisions, reproducibility, or auditability where deterministic behavior is required.","performance_implication":"Deterministic execution constraints may affect performance only when imp