{"record_id":"D49-B77-R002","dataset_id":"D49","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","batch":"B77","topic":"Flaky-Test Acceptance","subtopic":"Flaky-test exclusion control","concept":"A test identified as flaky must not automatically be treated as passing merely because it is classified as flaky.","knowledge_type":"CONSTRAINT","language":"English","language_version":"N/A","objective":"Prevent flakiness classification from bypassing substantive acceptance requirements.","requirements":["Flaky-test handling policy is explicit","Excluded tests have a defined replacement or disposition","Acceptance impact is explicit"],"constraints":["Flaky classification is not equivalent to PASS","Mandatory requirements cannot be silently removed"],"prerequisites":["Flaky-test policy","Requirement-to-test mapping","Acceptance decision rule"],"dependencies":["D49-B11-R002","D49-B68-R001"],"input":{"test_status":"FLAKY","requirement":"mandatory","replacement_test":"NONE"},"output":{"acceptance_status":"UNRESOLVED","reason":"mandatory_requirement_uncovered"},"expected_behavior":"Acceptance remains unresolved or fails when a mandatory requirement lacks valid verification after a test is excluded for flakiness.","correct_example":{"criterion":"A flaky test may be excluded only when the policy defines how the underlying requirement remains verified."},"incorrect_example":{"criterion":"PASS because the failing test was labeled flaky."},"correction":"Require a valid alternative verification path or explicit authorized acceptance state.","failure_mode":"Flaky-test suppression removes mandatory requirement coverage.","expected_error":"MANDATORY_REQUIREMENT_UNVERIFIED","security_implication":"Suppressing flaky security tests can leave security requirements unverified.","performance_implication":"Suppressing unstable performance tests can hide regressions; replacement measurement criteria may be required.","testing_method":"Mark a mandatory test flaky without providing replacement eviden