{"record_id":"D49-B77-R003","dataset_id":"D49","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","batch":"B77","topic":"Flaky-Test Acceptance","subtopic":"Flakiness evidence attribution","concept":"Flakiness decisions must be supported by execution evidence attributable to consistent relevant conditions.","knowledge_type":"VERIFICATION_RULE","language":"English","language_version":"N/A","objective":"Ensure flaky-test classifications are evidence-based.","requirements":["Execution history is available","Relevant environment and configuration are recorded","Failure and success outcomes are attributable"],"constraints":["Evidence from unrelated environments must not be combined without justification","Classification must follow the declared policy"],"prerequisites":["Execution records","Environment records","Flakiness policy"],"dependencies":["D49-B74-R005","D49-B13-R001"],"input":{"runs":[{"id":"R1","env":"A","result":"FAIL"},{"id":"R2","env":"B","result":"PASS"}],"same_conditions":false},"output":{"acceptance_status":"UNRESOLVED","reason":"conditions_not_comparable"},"expected_behavior":"Acceptance does not treat results from materially different conditions as sufficient evidence of flakiness unless the policy explicitly permits comparison.","correct_example":{"criterion":"PASS classification only when the evidence set satisfies the policy's comparability requirements."},"incorrect_example":{"criterion":"Classify as flaky whenever any two runs differ."},"correction":"Require comparable execution conditions or an explicit policy for cross-condition analysis.","failure_mode":"Condition changes are mistaken for nondeterministic test behavior.","expected_error":"FLAKINESS_EVIDENCE_NOT_COMPARABLE","security_implication":"Cross-environment mixing can obscure security-test failures specific to a vulnerable configuration.","performance_implication":"Different hardware or workload conditions can create apparent flakiness that is actually performance variance.","testing_method":"