{"record_id":"D49-B77-R004","dataset_id":"D49","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","batch":"B77","topic":"Flaky-Test Acceptance","subtopic":"Flaky-test remediation acceptance","concept":"A flaky-test remediation must be accepted only when the declared remediation requirement is verified and the underlying coverage remains adequate.","knowledge_type":"VERIFICATION_RULE","language":"English","language_version":"N/A","objective":"Verify that changes intended to reduce flakiness preserve test purpose and acceptance coverage.","requirements":["Remediation change is identified","Original failure condition is characterized","Post-remediation verification is defined","Requirement coverage is preserved"],"constraints":["A test becoming consistently passing does not by itself prove the product defect is fixed","Test weakening must not be treated as remediation success"],"prerequisites":["Flaky-test evidence","Remediation change","Acceptance criterion"],"dependencies":["D49-B67-R001","D49-B68-R001"],"input":{"pre_remediation":["PASS","FAIL","PASS"],"post_remediation":["PASS","PASS","PASS"],"coverage_preserved":true},"output":{"acceptance_status":"PASS"},"expected_behavior":"Remediation acceptance passes only when stability improves according to the declared criterion without weakening required verification coverage.","correct_example":{"criterion":"PASS when post-remediation evidence satisfies the stability requirement and the test continues to verify the intended requirement."},"incorrect_example":{"criterion":"PASS because assertions were removed and the test now always passes."},"correction":"Verify both stability and preservation of meaningful acceptance coverage.","failure_mode":"Flakiness is hidden by weakening or removing assertions.","expected_error":"FLAKY_TEST_REMEDIATION_UNVERIFIED","security_implication":"Weakening security assertions to remove flakiness can reduce actual security coverage.","performance_implication":"Removing timing assertions can conceal performance regressions.","testing_method":"Compare pre- and post-remediation assertions and repeated execution results.","test_input":{"assertion_strength":"preserved","post_runs":["PASS","PASS","PASS"]},"expected_test_result":"Acceptance passes only if required coverage remains intact and the defined stability condition is met.","verification_method":"Review change scope, assertion coverage, repeated results, and requirement traceability.","validation_status":"GENERATED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","provenance":"structured_requirement_acceptance_methodology","evidence_level":"METHODOLOGY","confidence":"HIGH","relationships":[{"type":"requires","target":"D49-B67-R001"},{"type":"requires","target":"D49-B68-R001"},{"type":"verifies","target":"D49-B77-R004"}],"related_records":["D49-B67-R001","D49-B68-R001"]}

{"record_id":"D49-B77-R005","dataset_id":"D49","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","batch":"B77","topic":"Flaky-Test Acceptance","subtopic":"Flaky-test decision auditability","concept":"A flaky-test acceptance decision must retain the evidence, classification rule, and resulting decision needed for later review.","knowledge_type":"VERIFICATION_RULE","language":"English","language_version":"N/A","objective":"Make flaky-test handling auditable and reproducible.","requirements":["Classification evidence is retained","Decision rule is identifiable","Acceptance impact is recorded"],"constraints":["Audit records must not claim evidence that was not collected","Sensitive test data must be handled according to applicable controls"],"prerequisites":["Flakiness policy","Execution evidence","Acceptance decision record"],"dependencies":["D49-B20-R005","D49-B24-R001"],"input":{"test":"T-A","classification":"FLAKY","evidence":"RUN-HISTORY","decision":"UNRESOLVED"},"output":{"acceptance_status":"PASS"},"expected_behavior":"The audit criterion passes when the classification and acceptance decision can be reconstructed from retained evidence.","correct_example":{"criterion":"PASS when execution history, classification rule, evidence, and acceptance impact are recorded and attributable."},"incorrect_example":{"criterion":"PASS because the test dashboard shows a flaky label."},"correction":"Require underlying evidence and decision metadata rather than relying on a display label.","failure_mode":"Flaky-test decisions cannot be independently reconstructed.","expected_error":"FLAKY_DECISION_AUDIT_GAP","security_implication":"Poor auditability can conceal suppression of security-test failures.","performance_implication":"Historical flaky-test evidence can help distinguish real performance variability from infrastructure noise.","testing_method":"Remove the classification rule or execution evidence and evaluate auditability.","test_input":{"classification_rule":null,"execution_h