{"record_id":"D49-B78-R001","dataset_id":"D49","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","batch":"B78","topic":"Statistical and Probabilistic Acceptance","subtopic":"Statistical acceptance criterion","concept":"A statistical acceptance criterion must define the population, sample or run requirements, metric, threshold, and decision rule needed to determine acceptance.","knowledge_type":"VERIFICATION_RULE","language":"English","language_version":"N/A","objective":"Make probabilistic acceptance criteria mathematically and operationally explicit.","requirements":["Population or sampling context is defined","Metric is defined","Threshold or decision rule is defined","Required evidence volume is defined"],"constraints":["A statistical threshold must not be invented when the requirement does not specify one","Sample results must not be generalized beyond the declared population without justification"],"prerequisites":["Statistical requirement","Metric definition","Sampling rule"],"dependencies":["D49-B16-R001","D49-B49-R001"],"input":{"metric":"p95_latency","threshold_ms":250,"observed_ms":210,"sample_count":1000},"output":{"acceptance_status":"PASS"},"expected_behavior":"Acceptance is determined using the declared statistical metric, threshold, and evidence conditions.","correct_example":{"criterion":"PASS when the declared metric computed over the required sample population satisfies the specified threshold and statistical decision rule."},"incorrect_example":{"criterion":"PASS because the average latency is below the threshold when the requirement specifies p95."},"correction":"Use the exact metric and statistical rule specified by the requirement.","failure_mode":"Incorrect metric or insufficient sampling produces an invalid acceptance decision.","expected_error":"STATISTICAL_CRITERION_UNDEFINED_OR_UNSATISFIED","security_implication":"Security acceptance based on incomplete statistical evidence may create false confidence.","performance_implication":"Statistical 