{"record_id":"D49-B78-R002","dataset_id":"D49","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","batch":"B78","topic":"Statistical and Probabilistic Acceptance","subtopic":"Sample sufficiency","concept":"Statistical acceptance requires the sample size or evidence quantity specified by the governing criterion to be satisfied before a decision is considered valid.","knowledge_type":"CONSTRAINT","language":"English","language_version":"N/A","objective":"Prevent insufficient samples from being treated as conclusive statistical evidence.","requirements":["Minimum sample requirement is defined","Observed sample count is known","Insufficient evidence produces a non-passing or unresolved state"],"constraints":["No universal sample size is assumed","Required sample size depends on the statistical method and requirement"],"prerequisites":["Statistical acceptance criterion","Sampling plan","Observed sample count"],"dependencies":["D49-B13-R001","D49-B78-R001"],"input":{"required_samples":1000,"observed_samples":200},"output":{"acceptance_status":"UNRESOLVED","reason":"sample_insufficient"},"expected_behavior":"Acceptance does not pass when the observed evidence volume is below the declared requirement.","correct_example":{"criterion":"PASS only when the minimum sample requirement and all other statistical conditions are satisfied."},"incorrect_example":{"criterion":"PASS because the available sample appears representative."},"correction":"Enforce the declared evidence quantity requirement.","failure_mode":"Under-sampled evidence is used for a definitive acceptance decision.","expected_error":"STATISTICAL_SAMPLE_INSUFFICIENT","security_implication":"Insufficient security-event samples may fail to expose rare behavior relevant to the requirement.","performance_implication":"Small samples can produce unstable performance estimates; no universal statistical guarantee is implied.","testing_method":"Evaluate acceptance using fewer samples than required.","test_input":{"required":1000,