":"Successful Projects","subtopic":"Scope Change During Delivery","concept":"Successful projects must preserve material scope changes because the final outcome may otherwise be evaluated against obsolete objectives.","knowledge_type":"CHANGE_CONTROL_RULE","objective":"Capture how project success should remain traceable when scope changes during implementation.","requirements":["Material scope changes must be recorded.","Affected requirements must be identifiable.","Final outcome must be evaluated against the applicable scope."],"constraints":["Do not silently replace the original scope.","Do not treat removed requirements as satisfied requirements."],"prerequisites":["Original scope","change records","final scope"],"dependencies":["D50-B02-R002","D50-B11-R001"],"input":"Original requirements, approved changes, and final scope.","output":"Change-aware success record.","expected_behavior":"The record distinguishes original objectives from changed or removed objectives.","failure_mode":"Final implementation is judged successful against a silently altered requirement set.","expected_error":"SCOPE_CHANGE_TRACEABILITY_LOST","security_implication":"Security requirements removed or weakened during delivery must remain visible.","performance_implication":"Changed workloads or capacity targets can invalidate earlier performance evidence.","testing_method":"Scope-change traceability review.","test_input":"Requirement removed during delivery without an explicit change record.","expected_test_result":"Requirement status is unresolved rather than silently satisfied.","verification_method":"Compare original and final requirement sets and their evidence.","validation_status":"GENERATED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","evidence_level":"METHODOLOGY","confidence":"HIGH","provenance":"operational_experience_dataset_methodology","relationships":["refines:D50-B02-R002"],"related_records":[]} {"record_id":"D50-B11-R005","dataset_id":"D50","batch_id":"B11","topic":"Successful Projects",