ity-control residual uncertainty","knowledge_type":"operational_engineering_evidence","objective":"Represent security controls that were present but not fully verified within the successful project evidence.","requirements":["Identify the control.","Record implementation evidence.","Record verification gap.","Record scope and assumptions."],"constraints":["Implemented, tested, and verified are separate states."],"input":"Security control implementation and available verification evidence.","output":"Explicit residual-security-uncertainty record.","expected_behavior":"Unverified portions remain visible to downstream reasoning and are not treated as established security facts.","failure_mode":"Implemented controls are incorrectly labeled fully verified.","root_cause":"State conflation between implementation and verification.","testing_method":"Attempt to trace the control from implementation through test and verification evidence.","test_input":"Control implementation and available test records.","expected_test_result":"Verification state is accurately classified.","verification_method":"Review evidence-state transitions.","security_implication":"Unverified controls remain risk-relevant until evidence is obtained.","validation_status":"REQUIRES_PROJECT_SPECIFIC_EVIDENCE","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","provenance":["NIST SP 800-53","OWASP ASVS"],"relationships":[{"type":"refines","record_id":"D50-B67-R001"},{"type":"contrasts_with","record_id":"D50-B67-R002"}]} {"record_id":"D50-B68-R001","dataset_id":"D50","topic":"Successful Projects","subtopic":"Scalability","concept":"Capacity-bound success evidence","knowledge_type":"operational_engineering_evidence","objective":"Record the workload boundary under which a project outcome was successfully demonstrated.","requirements":["Identify workload dimensions.","Record observed or declared capacity boundary.","Record resource conditions.","Separate measured capacity from design target."],"constraints":["A successful low-load test does not establish behavior at higher load."],"input":"Workload, resource measurements, capacity result, acceptance criteria.","output":"Bounded capacity evidence.","expected_behavior":"The success claim is associated only with the workload and resource conditions actually evaluated.","failure_mode":"Success at one workload is generalized to all expected workloads.","root_cause":"Missing load boundary or unsupported extrapolation.","testing_method":"Execute representative load tests appropriate to the project.","test_input":"Defined workload profile and resource boundary.","expected_test_result":"Acceptance criteria are satisfied at the tested workload.","verification_method":"Review workload definition, measurements, and acceptance criteria.","performance_implication":"Capacity values must be labeled MEASURED when actually measured and ESTIMATED/INFERRED otherwise.","validation_status":"REQUIRES_PROJECT_SPECIFIC_EVIDENCE","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","provenance":["ISO/IEC/IEEE 25010:2023","ISO/IEC/IEEE 29119"],"relationships":[{"type":"extends","record_id":"D50-B56-R001"},{"type":"related_to","record_id":"D50-B68-R003"}]} {"record_id":"D50-B68-R002","dataset_id":"D50","topic":"Successful Projects","subtopic":"Scalability","concept":"Scaling-mode evidence","knowledge_type":"operational_engineering_evidence","objective":"Distinguish horizontal, vertical, partitioned, queued, cached, or other scaling behavior when recording successful project evidence.","requirements":["Identify scaling mechanism.","Identify bottleneck being addressed.","Record tested boundary.","Record functional invariants that must remain satisfied."],"constraints":["Different scaling modes have different failure and consistency characteristics."],"input":"Scaling implementation, workload, measurements, and functional checks.","output":"Scaling-mode-specific success evidence.","expected_behavior":"Scaling preserves required behavior within the tested boundary.","failure_mode":"Resource capacity increases while correctness, consistency, latency, or reliability degrades beyond acceptance limits.","root_cause":"Scaling mechanism changes system behavior or exposes a different bottleneck.","testing_method":"Evaluate the selected scaling mode under representative workload increments.","test_input":"Baseline workload and increased workload profiles.","expected_test_result":"Declared capacity and functional acceptance criteria remain satisfied.","verification_method":"Compare workload, resource, correctness, and performance evidence across scaling levels.","performance_implication":"No numerical scaling benefit may be claimed without measurements.","validation_status":"REQUIRES_PROJECT_SPECIFIC_EVIDENCE","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","provenance":["ISO/IEC/IEEE 25010:2023","Google SRE literature"],"relationships":[{"type":"specializes","record_id":"D50-B68-R001"},{"type":"related_to","record_id":"D50-B64-R003"}]} {"record_id":"D50-B68-R003","dataset_id":"D50","topic":"Successful Projects","subtopic":"Scalability","concept":"Bottleneck transition evidence","knowledge_type":"operational_engineering_evidence","objective":"Record whether scaling shifts the dominant bottleneck rather than eliminating all capacity constraints.","requirements":["Measure relevant resource or service constraints.","Compare baseline and scaled conditions.","Identify the limiting component under each condition."],"constraints":["A new bottleneck after scaling is not necessarily evidence that scaling failed."],"input":"Baseline and scaled workload measurements.","output":"Bottleneck transition record.","expected_behavior":"The evidence identifies the limiting resource or dependency at each tested boundary.","failure_mode":"A single bottleneck explanation is incorrectly applied after the system architecture changes under load.","root_cause":"Incomplete capacity analysis.","testing_method":"Repeat workload evaluation while observing relevant resource dimensions.","test_input":"Multiple workload levels.","expected_test_result":"Observed bottleneck transitions are identified or no transition is observed within the tested boundary.","verification_method":"Correlate workload with resource saturation and outcome metrics.","performance_implication":"All numerical claims require measured or clearly labeled estimated evidence.","validation_status":"REQUIRES_PROJECT_SPECIFIC_EVIDENCE","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","provenance":["Google SRE literature","ISO/IEC/IEEE 25010:2023"],"relationships":[{"type":"refines","record_id":"D50-B68-R001"},{"type":"causes","record_id":"D50-B68-R004"}]} {"record_id":"D50-B68-R004","dataset_id":"D50","topic":"Successful Projects","subtopic":"Scalability","concept":"Graceful degradation evidence","knowledge_type":"operational_engineering_evidence","objective":"Capture behavior when workload or resource availability exceeds the demonstrated normal operating boundary.","requirements":["Define overload conditions.","Define acceptable degraded behavior.","Record rejection, queuing, throttling, fallback, or failure behavior.","Record recovery after overload."],"constraints":["Graceful degradation must be evidenced for the specific overload modes claimed."],"input":"Overload scenario, system behavior, resource observations, recovery result.","output":"Overload-behavior evidence.","expected_behavior":"The system follows its declared degraded-mode behavior without violating critical invariants.","failure_mode":"Overload produces uncontrolled cascading failure or corrupt state.","root_cause":"Missing capacity controls, poor isolation, or untested overload behavior.","testing_method":"Exercise controlled overload conditions and validate degraded-mode criteria.","test_input":"Workload above declared normal capacity.","expected_test_result":"Declared degradation behavior occurs and critical invariants remain satisfied.","verification_method":"Review telemetry, functional results, and recovery evidence.","security_implication"