nce must be separated from throughput/latency measurements.","validation_status":"REQUIRES_PROJECT_SPECIFIC_EVIDENCE","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","provenance":["ISO/IEC/IEEE 25010:2023","ISO/IEC/IEEE 29119"],"relationships":[{"type":"verifies","record_id":"D50-B68-R002"},{"type":"extends","record_id":"D50-B68-R004"}]} {"record_id":"D50-B69-R001","dataset_id":"D50","topic":"Successful Projects","subtopic":"Handoff","concept":"Operational handoff completeness","knowledge_type":"operational_engineering_evidence","objective":"Capture whether a successful project can be transferred into defined ownership or operational responsibility.","requirements":["Identify receiving role or team.","Provide operational prerequisites.","Provide deployment and recovery procedures.","Provide monitoring and escalation information.","Record handoff validation."],"constraints":["Handoff documentation alone does not prove operational readiness."],"input":"Project artifact, operational documentation, receiving team, handoff task.","output":"Validated handoff evidence.","expected_behavior":"The receiving operator can perform defined operational tasks within the declared boundary.","failure_mode":"The project is technically complete but cannot be operated safely by the receiving party.","root_cause":"Missing operational knowledge, access prerequisites, monitoring, or recovery procedures.","testing_method":"Conduct a structured handoff exercise with representative operational tasks.","test_input":"Project package and defined operational task set.","expected_test_result":"Receiving party completes mandatory tasks according to acceptance criteria.","verification_method":"Record task outcomes, unresolved questions, and required assistance.","validation_status":"REQUIRES_PROJECT_SPECIFIC_EVIDENCE","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","provenance":["ISO/IEC/IEEE 12207:2017","ISO/IEC/IEEE 25010:2023"],"relationships":[{"type":"extends","record_id":"D50-B66-R004"},{"type":"related_to","record_id":"