es","concept":"Acceptance-criteria integrity","knowledge_type":"verification_evidence","objective":"Ensure that successful project claims are evaluated against criteria defined before or independently of the observed result where possible.","requirements":["Identify acceptance criteria.","Record criterion origin and timestamp.","Record observed result.","Prevent post-hoc criterion rewriting without traceability."],"constraints":["Criteria may legitimately evolve, but changes must remain versioned and attributable."],"input":"Acceptance criteria and observed project result.","output":"Versioned acceptance assessment.","expected_behavior":"The system can determine which criteria were used to classify the outcome.","failure_mode":"Criteria are changed after observing the result to make success appear established.","root_cause":"Uncontrolled acceptance-criteria lifecycle.","testing_method":"Compare criterion versions with execution and decision timestamps.","test_input":"Original and revised acceptance criteria.","expected_test_result":"The classification uses the appropriate criterion version and preserves later changes.","verification_method":"Temporal traceability audit.","validation_status":"REQUIRES_PROJECT_SPECIFIC_EVIDENCE","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","provenance":["ISO/IEC/IEEE 29119","ISO/IEC/IEEE 12207:2017"],"relationships":[{"type":"requires","record_id":"D50-B74-R001"},{"type":"related_to","record_id":"D50-B72-R001"}]} {"record_id":"D50-B74-R003","dataset_id":"D50","topic":"Successful Projects","subtopic":"Quality Outcomes","concept":"Quality-attribute balance","knowledge_type":"quality_engineering_evidence","objective":"Represent successful project outcomes across relevant quality attributes instead of collapsing them into a single success value.","requirements":["Identify relevant quality attributes.","Record evidence per attribute.","Record trade-offs.","Preserve unresolved attributes."],"constraints":["A numerical overall quality score must not be