come validation.","testing_method":"Execute representative end-to-end user workflows.","test_input":"Representative user scenarios.","expected_test_result":"Declared user acceptance criteria pass.","verification_method":"Trace user outcome to end-to-end evidence.","validation_status":"REQUIRES_PROJECT_SPECIFIC_EVIDENCE","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","provenance":["ISO/IEC/IEEE 25010:2023","ISO/IEC/IEEE 29119"],"relationships":[{"type":"extends","record_id":"D50-B63-R001"},{"type":"related_to","record_id":"D50-B74-R001"}]} {"record_id":"D50-B74-R005","dataset_id":"D50","topic":"Successful Projects","subtopic":"Quality Outcomes","concept":"Outcome durability evidence","knowledge_type":"longitudinal_operational_evidence","objective":"Determine whether a successful project outcome persists beyond the initial acceptance window.","requirements":["Define durability observation period.","Identify outcome indicators.","Record subsequent material changes.","Record degradation or preservation of the outcome."],"constraints":["Long-term durability cannot be claimed when the observation period is insufficient.","Durability evidence is contextual and time-bounded."],"input":"Initial success evidence, longitudinal observations, subsequent changes.","output":"Time-bounded durability assessment.","expected_behavior":"The record distinguishes initial success from sustained success.","failure_mode":"Short-term success is treated as durable without longitudinal evidence.","root_cause":"Observation window not defined or evidence not retained.","testing_method":"Re-evaluate outcome indicators after the declared observation interval.","test_input":"Successful project and longitudinal monitoring data.","expected_test_result":"Durability classification reflects actual observations.","verification_method":"Compare outcome state across the defined time window.","performance_implication":"Longitudinal performance claims require actual observations for the stated period.","validation_status